<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Additional Results of Small-Scale Experiments</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we provide details of the small-scale experimental results that could not be included in the main paper.
In particular, we investigate the goodness of approximation of the information matrix in the small-scale case, since it can be computed exactly, although the execution time is longer.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.2.1 </span>Empirical Relationship between H and F</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we examine the behavior of <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{H}(\bm{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{H}(\bm{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> when it is approximated by <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}(\bm{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}(\bm{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>, or more precisely, <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}_{\text{1mc}}(\bm{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑭</mi><mtext>1mc</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}_{\text{1mc}}(\bm{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Figure <a href="#A4.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ D.2.1 Empirical Relationship between H and F ‣ D.2 Additional Results of Small-Scale Experiments ‣ Appendix D Additional Experimental Results ‣ Takeuchi’s Information Criteria as a Generalization Measure for Deep Neural Networks Close to the NTK Regime" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> shows that <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{H}(\bm{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{H}(\bm{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> is not in perfect agreement with <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}(\bm{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}(\bm{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> due to the effect of the damping term.
However, for cases that do not require inverse calculations, such as trace calculations and lower bounds, these effects can be eliminated and a relatively good approximation can be achieved.
Furthermore, in the case of linear neural networks, <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{H}(\bm{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{H}(\bm{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}(\bm{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}(\bm{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> show a strong correlation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F9" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.23219v1/v_exact_tic_h_vs_v_exact_tic_f.svg" id="A4.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:247/170;" width="247" height="170"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.23219v1/v_block_diag_tic_h_vs_v_block_diag_tic_f.svg" id="A4.F9.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:247/171;" width="247" height="171"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.23219v1/v_diag_tic_h_vs_v_diag_tic_f.svg" id="A4.F9.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:247/178;" width="247" height="178"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.23219v1/v_fast_tic_h_vs_v_fast_tic_f.svg" id="A4.F9.g4" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:247/169;" width="247" height="169"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.23219v1/x2.svg" id="A4.F9.g5" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:247/174;" width="247" height="174"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>Small-scale experiments: comparison of the TIC estimate w/ <math id="A4.F9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{H}(\bm{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{H}(\bm{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.F9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}(\bm{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}(\bm{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>. Dataset: TinyMNIST. </figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.2.2 </span>Effect of Matrix Shape Approximation on Estimation of TIC</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we fixed the use of <math id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{F}(\bm{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{F}(\bm{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> rather than <math id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{H}(\bm{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜽</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{H}(\bm{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math> and observed the change in the TIC estimates and the correlation with the generalization gap when the form of the matrix is changed by the approximation method.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figures <a href="#A4.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ D.2.2 Effect of Matrix Shape Approximation on Estimation of TIC ‣ D.2 Additional Results of Small-Scale Experiments ‣ Appendix D Additional Experimental Results ‣ Takeuchi’s Information Criteria as a Generalization Measure for Deep Neural Networks Close to the NTK Regime" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> and <a href="#A4.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ D.2.2 Effect of Matrix Shape Approximation on Estimation of TIC ‣ D.2 Additional Results of Small-Scale Experiments ‣ Appendix D Additional Experimental Results ‣ Takeuchi’s Information Criteria as a Generalization Measure for Deep Neural Networks Close to the NTK Regime" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> show the correlation between the TIC estimates and the generalized gaps in the case of approximation.
Figure <a href="#A4.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ D.2.2 Effect of Matrix Shape Approximation on Estimation of TIC ‣ D.2 Additional Results of Small-Scale Experiments ‣ Appendix D Additional Experimental Results ‣ Takeuchi’s Information Criteria as a Generalization Measure for Deep Neural Networks Close to the NTK Regime" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> shows a comparison of the shape of matrix and its estimates, and Figure <a href="#A4.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ D.2.2 Effect of Matrix Shape Approximation on Estimation of TIC ‣ D.2 Additional Results of Small-Scale Experiments ‣ Appendix D Additional Experimental Results ‣ Takeuchi’s Information Criteria as a Generalization Measure for Deep Neural Networks Close to the NTK Regime" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> shows the correlation between generalization gap and TIC estimates.
These values are evaluated using three different correlation metric and summarized in Tables <a href="#A4.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ D.2.2 Effect of Matrix Shape Approximation on Estimation of TIC ‣ D.2 Additional Results of Small-Scale Experiments ‣ Appendix D Additional Experimental Results ‣ Takeuchi’s Information Criteria as a Generalization Measure for Deep Neural Networks Close to the NTK Regime" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, <a href="#A4.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ D.2.2 Effect of Matrix Shape Approximation on Estimation of TIC ‣ D.2 Additional Results of Small-Scale Experiments ‣ Appendix D Additional Experimental Results ‣ Takeuchi’s Information Criteria as a Generalization Measure for Deep Neural Networks Close to the NTK Regime" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, and <a href="#A4.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ D.2.2 Effect of Matrix Shape Approximation on Estimation of TIC ‣ D.2 Additional Results of Small-Scale Experiments ‣ Appendix D Additional Experimental Results ‣ Takeuchi’s Information Criteria as a Generalization Measure for Deep Neural Networks Close to the NTK Regime" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>.</p>
</div>
